# See corpus/laravel/endpoints for the format. PrestaShop has no public/ dir:
# the docroot is the install root itself, same as WordPress.
#
# database is "mysql:<host>:<port>:<dbname>" rather than a sqlite file path --
# the only app in this corpus with an external database server (TCP loopback,
# not a socket: see db-up.sh for why). verify.sh starts mariadbd against
# ${app}/db-data before this line is checked and stops it after the app's
# http server is killed; see corpus/prestashop/db-up.sh and db-down.sh, and
# task-29a-report.md for why the DB engine cannot be sqlite (PrestaShop's
# ObjectModel/Db layer requires MySQL/MariaDB SQL dialect).
#
# Front-office only (TTFB is what PGO is training for). Back-office/admin is
# deliberately not here: the installer randomizes the admin folder name for
# security on every run (src/PrestaShopBundle/Install/Install.php finalize()),
# so it is not a fixed path the way the brief asks for -- adding it would mean
# either disabling that security behaviour in the corpus (a real PrestaShop
# never ships that way) or hand-renaming the folder back to something fixed
# per build, and it is not cheap: nothing else in this corpus needs a second,
# stateful rename step at build time. All demo IDs below are PrestaShop's own
# fixtures ("Hummingbird" theme + demo catalog), read out of the installed
# ps_category/ps_product/ps_product_attribute/ps_cms tables after a real
# install -- not guessed.
#
# PS_REWRITING_SETTINGS is forced to 0 after install (see db-up.sh's install
# step) so these query-string URLs are canonical and PrestaShop does not 302
# them to a rewritten path that php -S (no router, no mod_rewrite) would then
# 404 on. Even so PrestaShop 302s once to reorder its own query string
# (?controller=x&id_y=n -> ?id_y=n&controller=x); verify.sh/train.sh follow
# redirects (curl -L) for every app because of this, not only for prestashop.
#
# One file serves every PrestaShop the tiers pin (9.2.0, 8.2.8, 1.7.8.11,
# 1.6.1.24), so an expected substring may list alternatives separated by '|':
# 1.6's demo catalogue puts Women/Tops/"Faded Short Sleeves T-shirt"/"Printed
# Dress" at the same IDs where 1.7+ has Clothes/Accessories/Hummingbird/Framed
# poster. There is no cart path: no single URL renders an empty cart on all
# four (1.6 shows it on controller=order, 1.7+ on cart&action=show, and each
# sends the other's URL to the home page), so the listing controller
# new-products stands in for it -- same title on every version.
# id_category=6 is optional: 1.6's corpus install 404s it (its demo data
# nests the second "Tops" differently), and 1.7+ still have to render
# Accessories there whenever it answers 200.
docroot .
# PrestaShop is not itself a composer package (it is the root project), so
# this is a third version kind alongside "composer" and "wordpress" --
# verify.sh reads install/install_version.php's _PS_INSTALL_VERSION_
# constant, which is why the Dockerfile keeps that one file instead of
# deleting install/ the way the official upstream entrypoint does.
version prestashop install/install_version.php
database mysql:127.0.0.1:13306:prestashop SELECT COUNT(*) FROM ps_product WHERE active = 1
# Overrides verify.sh/train.sh's shared negative-control path (task 29e).
# PrestaShop has no path router at all with rewriting off -- ?controller= is
# the only thing index.php dispatches on -- so a bare nonexistent path always
# renders the catalog home (200) once it reaches index.php, and whether it
# reaches index.php is a PHP-built-in-server routing detail that measurably
# differs between PHP versions this same tier serves (8.2 404s an unmatched
# path with an extension at the server level; 8.4 forwards it to index.php
# regardless). A garbage ?controller= value sidesteps that entirely: it always
# reaches index.php (it's a query string on a real file, not a routed path),
# and PrestaShop's own dispatcher 404s a controller it cannot resolve --
# confirmed by hand, and true regardless of the built-in server's version.
negative-control /index.php?controller=corpus-negative-control-4f21a9
path / required 4096 PrestaShop
path /index.php?controller=category&id_category=3 required 4096 Clothes|Women
path /index.php?controller=category&id_category=6 optional 4096 Accessories|Tops
path /index.php?controller=product&id_product=1 required 4096 Hummingbird printed t-shirt|Faded Short Sleeves T-shirt
path /index.php?controller=product&id_product=3 required 4096 Framed poster|Printed Dress
path /index.php?controller=search&s=shirt required 2048 Search
path /index.php?controller=cms&id_cms=3 required 2048 Terms and conditions of use
path /index.php?controller=contact required 2048 Contact us
path /index.php?controller=auth required 2048 Login
path /index.php?controller=new-products required 4096 New products
